From 2c8449fe24da34becb9485a94e746bbaeda5aa55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: n64recomp-shaders <n64recomp-shaders@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:40:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Widescreen borders: pillarbox border canvas renderer + C
 API

WidescreenBorders draws an RGBA canvas (side + game + side columns, center
transparent) around the game image when the window is wider than the game
(Original aspect ratio). Reuses VIRenderer (viewport/scissor/gamma overrides),
so no new shaders. Shader scope: GameOnly (default; borders drawn unprocessed)
or GameAndBorders (canvas + game composed at the game's internal row
resolution, then the post-process preset runs on the composite).
C API: rt64_widescreen_{supported,set_enabled,is_enabled,set_canvas,
set_shader_scope,get_shader_scope,set_filter}. New files are MIT.
